id: pm-rl-github-eecd7460423f-202
title: Make the packed LM CLI proof budget follow the test profile
description: "Tracks https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/issues/202. The quick Node 26 coverage shard exhausted the packed LM subprocess watchdog after producing a valid rejection receipt."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#202"
created_at: "2026-11-26T01:29:59.078Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-26T03:57:19.481Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Scale the wall-clock watchdog with the test profile.; Always verify three generations and the persisted contamination refusal.; Prove a subprocess exceeding its scaled watchdog still fails.
comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T01:30:07.354Z",codex-agent,Read issue #202 and its comment. The original CI job failed on the Node 26 coverage shard at the reported 27.3 s while producing the expected evaluation_rejected result. Reproducing the focused instrumented test against the unchanged checkout and auditing other fixed 20-second subprocess watchdogs.
  "2026-11-26T01:30:54.141Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced unchanged under targeted Node 26.13.0 V8 coverage at quick depth: 0/1 passed, ETIMEDOUT after 30.989 s total. The hosted Node 26.13.1 log confirms a 25-second subprocess watchdog (despite the former test title), SIGTERM and a valid evaluation_rejected receipt. The evaluation-plan 100k fence scan has the remaining fixed 20-second child watchdog. Plan: preserve their actual ordinary-run limits, scale their budgets for V8 coverage and explicit deep profiles, and exercise a real over-budget child."
  "2026-11-26T01:33:06.790Z",codex-agent,"The test-only proof runner preserves a finite watchdog: 2x under V8 coverage, with explicit PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE taking precedence. The LM watchdog stays at its 25-second ordinary baseline and the scan keeps its 20-second subprocess and two-second inner scan baselines. The LM acceptance also verifies the persisted comment text on the approval item."
  "2026-11-26T01:37:11.152Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs on Node 26: the unchanged packed LM reproducer failed 0/1 with ETIMEDOUT. With a controlled 21.5 s startup delay, restoring only the scan child 20 s watchdog failed with ETIMEDOUT while the fixed call completed in 23.154 s. Removing the V8 coverage multiplier failed the profile matrix; bypassing the scale timed out the within-budget subprocess; removing the watchdog failed with Missing expected exception after the child printed its receipt. In the scratch packed LM proof, suppressing just the approval audit append failed the persisted refusal assertion, and giving the real programme only two generations failed the 3-generation assertion. The focused fixed Node 26 V8 run passed 47/47; its packed LM child completed in 42.982 s. Bun passed both watchdog regression tests."
  "2026-11-26T01:37:20.592Z",codex-agent,"Local targeted gates passed: source and test typechecks, build, lint, zero duplicate blocks, identity audit (5 approved addresses), and strict tracker health. All three linked pm test commands passed (2 harness tests, 37 identity/changelog tests, 45 LM/evaluation tests; zero failed, skipped or cancelled). A focused instrumented run passed 47/47 and direct Bun watchdog tests passed 2/2. Full coverage and release checks are delegated to exact-head CI."
  "2026-11-26T01:57:54.885Z",codex-agent,"Exact PR #205 head a6acf9447cc8c506bd271b33c119c2f83d21d2c5 passed all 11 CI jobs before the cutoff. The original failing coverage shard passed 434/434 and the packed LM child completed in 11.848 s. Coverage merge reported 65 source files and 100% statements, lines, branches and functions. Node 22 and 26 aggregates, packed npm/Node and Bun release checks, and CodeQL passed. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45737088609 CodeQL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45737088606 . This local receipt leaves the certified PR head intact."
  "2026-11-26T02:21:46.124Z",pi-glm,"Re-review round 1 (auto) posted one non-blocking CodeRabbit finding on test/proof-budget.test.ts:43 — keep the outer watchdog above the nested proof budget at small scales. Verified valid: at a valid explicit PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE of 0.4 the outer testTime(10_000) drops to 4,000 ms while the nested regression needs at least 4,200 ms (1,200 ms within-budget proof plus the child-forced 3x watchdog of 3,000 ms), so the outer execFileSync kills the test although the code is correct; depth validation accepts any finite scale above zero. General rule: a harness watchdog that guards nested proof work whose budget is independent of the outer scale (child-forced scale, self-set V8 coverage, fixed nested sleeps) never scales below its declared unscaled budget."
  "2026-11-26T02:21:52.046Z",pi-glm,"Class sweep: the only outer watchdogs around nested independently-budgeted proof children are the two outer execFileSync watchdogs in test/proof-budget.test.ts — line 43 (the flagged one) and the same-shaped line 23, whose nested budget is instrumented child startup (a valid 0.01-scale run gives it 100 ms, below the measured ~130 ms). Product code never reads the harness scale and scripts use fixed unscaled timeouts, so no SDK/CLI instance exists. Must-allow corpus: test/lm-cli.test.ts and test/evaluation-plan.test.ts launch runTimedProof children with no outer scaled watchdog (their children inherit the suite scale), and test/depth.test.ts guards scale-forcing children with a plain unscaled 30,000 ms. Fix: outerProofTime(ms) = Math.max(ms, testTime(ms)) exported from test/support/proof-budget.ts with a docstring, used for both outer watchdogs; higher scales keep the larger budgets, and the two pre-existing tests are unchanged."
  "2026-11-26T02:21:53.369Z",pi-glm,"Two new tests close the class: a property matrix proving outerProofTime keeps the unscaled floor at scale 0.4, is unchanged at 1, preserves 3x deep budgets, and never drops below testTime for a 1..250,000 ms sweep; and an adversarial runner that re-runs the whole file as a child at explicit scale 0.005 with a reentrancy-guard env and asserts the child still passes (NODE_TEST_CONTEXT must be dropped from the child env — an empty string makes node:test skip file execution). Revert proofs in disposable copies at default scale: reverting only line 43 to testTime failed the adversarial test with child ETIMEDOUT (3 pass/1 fail); reverting only line 23 failed the adversarial test (the instrumented child outlives the 50 ms watchdog); removing the outerProofTime floor failed both new tests (value mismatch at 0.4 plus child ETIMEDOUT) while the two pre-existing tests stayed green in every case. The restored implementation passed 4/4 after each revert, plus 4/4 under V8 coverage, 4/4 at deep scale 3, and the packed consumers passed 45/45 after a build."
  "2026-11-26T02:24:15.697Z",pi-glm,"pm test --run selected all four linked commands and every one passed: the proof-budget file 4/4 at default scale, 37/37 tracker and identity tests, 45/45 packed lm-cli and evaluation-plan consumers (after a build), and the new whole-file run at explicit scale 0.4 passed 4/4 in 10.7 s. Local gates also passed: typecheck, lint at zero warnings, docstring gate over 577 declarations, zero duplicate blocks, the git identity audit over 5 approved addresses, and strict tracker health with merge drivers."
  "2026-11-26T02:30:24.464Z",pi-glm,"Transparency note on the fix commit: the first push of the outer-watchdog fix carried a mistyped commit identity (the noreply address with the wrong local-part spelling), which the CI git identity audit rejected in 31 s. The commit was amended to the approved address (verified byte-exact over the whole branch range) and re-pushed as a forced update of this PR branch; the reachable history now contains only approved addresses. The pre-amend duplicate remains as one unreachable, unanchored object inside the shared local pack until the next natural gc (fresh CI clones never contain it, and the identity gate passed on the amended head); a manual gc at a quiet moment can remove it sooner."
  "2026-11-26T02:48:33.853Z",pi-glm,"Exact head 10ad713 passed the full CI board well inside the cutoff: four quick Node 22 shards, four Node 26 coverage shards, coverage merge, quick release checks (including the git identity audit), both test aggregates and CodeQL all green at unchanged thresholds. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45742758904 CodeQL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45742758830 . The outer-watchdog fix and both revert-proof tests ride in commit 10ad713; the review thread at test/proof-budget.test.ts line 43 is answered by that commit with the property matrix and the adversarial whole-file child run as the tests that fail on revert."
  "2026-11-26T03:26:14.685Z",pi-glm,"Re-review round 2 (auto) posted one non-blocking CodeRabbit finding on test/proof-budget.test.ts:76 — spawn the whole-file regression with a runner the active runtime supports. Verified valid with the local bun binary: the watchdog regressions pass under bun test, but the whole-file child invoked as bun --test exits 1 with 'Cannot use test outside of the test runner', so the adversarial test fails before exercising the regressions. Two deeper bun incompatibilities surfaced while fixing: bun's node:test shim ignores the options-object skip (the reentrancy guard would recurse) and defaults every test to a 5-second timeout, which the 4.4-second watchdog regression and the ~5.5-second whole-file child both exceed. Probes confirmed bun honors the options-object timeout. Rule: a nested whole-file runner invocation must use a launch form the active runtime supports, and the reentrancy guard must not depend on runner-specific skip semantics."
  "2026-11-26T03:26:21.982Z",pi-glm,"Fix: testFileRunnerArguments(file) exported from test/support/proof-budget.ts selects node --test --test-concurrency=1 for Node runs and bun test for Bun runs; the whole-file regression spawns process.execPath with those arguments. The reentrancy guard keeps the skip option for Node reporting (the child still reports 1 skipped under node) and also returns early when the guard env is set, so runtimes that ignore skip semantics cannot recurse. The watchdog regression carries an explicit floored 30-second timeout and the whole-file regression a floored 90-second timeout, lifting bun's 5-second default while leaving Node behavior unchanged. The property matrix now also asserts the runner mode matches the active runtime. Class sweep: the node-only --test spawn is the established node-tier harness pattern (coverage-gate and quick-shards scripts, causal-proof and transfer-revert fixtures, transfer-review, lm-compose and training-influence child runs) — CI executes all of those under Node, including the bun release cell, which runs the suite through npm and node; only this proof file has an established direct-bun validation practice (the round-1 owner verification ran the watchdog tests under bun, and the new recorded bun command keeps that path certified). The other call sites are the must-allow corpus, not bun-run surface, so they keep the node-tier invocation."
  "2026-11-26T03:26:23.545Z",pi-glm,"Revert proof in a disposable copy with the runner selection reverted to node-only arguments: under bun the whole-file regression failed in 135 ms with the runner-start refusal (3 pass / 1 fail) while node stayed 4/4, proving the revert breaks exactly the runtime the finding names. Restored implementation: node 4/4, bun 4/4 with the child run completing in 4.6 s, the node child still reporting the guard skip, and the bun child finishing 4/4 with no recursion. Both the node-only revert (caught by the recorded bun run) and a bun-only-everywhere revert (caught by the runtime-mode assertion in the property matrix) fail a gate."
  "2026-11-26T03:29:44.482Z",pi-glm,"pm test --run over the five linked commands: the proof-budget file 4/4 under node (10.9 s) and 4/4 under bun (9.2 s), the whole file at explicit scale 0.4 4/4 (11.1 s), and 37/37 tracker and identity tests. The packed consumer command failed once in this round for an environmental reason — the end-of-round cleanup had removed the built output the packed archive embeds — and passed 45/45 in 67.4 s immediately after a rebuild, with no code change between the two runs."
  "2026-11-26T03:57:16.279Z",pi-glm,"Exact head a384e5c at the 30-minute cutoff: all four Node 26 coverage shards passed (13m02s/5m14s/13m19s/8m46s), the quick release checks passed including the git identity audit, and CodeQL passed. Pending at cutoff: the three Node 22 quick shards (queued on hosted runners, zero elapsed) and the coverage merge that waits on them. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45749373507 CodeQL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/45749373646 . The runtime-supported runner fix rides in commit a384e5c; the review thread at test/proof-budget.test.ts line 76 is answered by that commit, with the recorded bun run and the runtime-mode property assertion as the tests that fail on revert."
